From af38c70a465e4d1265878b3758300064b22141b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:52:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add typed structured events with a field registry

Capture core metadata and the actual caller automatically. Compile-time field
keys carry reviewed types and standard-name mappings; free-form/runtime keys
are rejected. Producer records carry IDs and bounded binary values; the logger
thread renders text/JSON and maps field names. Preserve disabled-category
short-circuiting, reference lifetime, marked truncation and auxiliary JSON
sink operation.

Include the original event-name escaping, caller-source, endpoint-role,
typed-key/lint and severe-overflow corrections at their introducing API.
Structured errors share the generic consumer acknowledgment fence. Raw WSS
address packing retains the full allowed payload where the record fits and
marks oversized records explicitly; it does not silently truncate addresses.
Later RpcUser IDs remain appended at the RPC conversion consumer.

Existing allocation probes cover their recorded warmed typed paths with
positive allocation controls. Legacy formatting/caller-created objects, cold
thread preparation and rare consumer emergency rendering have distinct costs.
This replaces the original WIP handover message; it is not a new performance,
full-suite or native-integration claim.

